/-!
# The Čech complex of a pro-covering is a resolution for injective sheaves

Let `J` be a Grothendieck topology on a category `C`, let `P` be a property of objects closed
under precomposition (if `B' ⟶ B` and `P B` then `P B'`), and let `T` be a simplicial object of
`ℕ ⥤ C` — a simplicial system of towers `T(n)_0 ⟶ T(n)_1 ⟶ ⋯` — all of whose members
`T(n)_e` have property `P`.  For an abelian presheaf `F` this file forms the cosimplicial group
`n ↦ lim_e F(T(n)_e)`, its alternating coface complex `sectionsComplex T F`, the sections
`Γ_P(F) = lim_{B ∈ P} F(B)` of `F` over `P` (`sectionsOver`), and the augmentation
`Γ_P(F) ⟶ lim_e F(T(0)_e)`, and proves that for an injective abelian sheaf `H` the augmented
complex

`0 ⟶ Γ_P(H) ⟶ lim_e H(T(0)_e) ⟶ lim_e H(T(1)_e) ⟶ lim_e H(T(2)_e) ⟶ ⋯`

is exact, under the following hypotheses relative to a property `𝒜` of "nice" objects:

* `h𝒜` (`𝒜`-objects cover): for every `B`, the sieve generated by the morphisms `B' ⟶ B` with
  `𝒜 B'` is a covering sieve;
* `hT₁` (local existence of maps): every `B` with `𝒜 B` and `P B` admits a morphism
  `B ⟶ T(0)_e` for some `e`;
* `hT₂` (pro-products): every `B` with `𝒜 B` satisfies `IsProProductAt T B`, namely
  - (existence) for all `n`, `e` and `φ i : B ⟶ T(0)_e` (`i : Fin (n + 1)`) there are `e' ≥ e`
    and `ψ : B ⟶ T(n)_{e'}` with `ψ ≫ T(const i)_{e'} = φ i ≫ T(0)(e ≤ e')` for every `i`,
    where `const i : ⦋0⦌ ⟶ ⦋n⦌` is the `i`-th vertex;
  - (uniqueness) two morphisms `ψ ψ' : B ⟶ T(n)_e` with `ψ ≫ T(const i)_e = ψ' ≫ T(const i)_e`
    for every `i` agree after composing with `T(n)(e ≤ e')` for some `e' ≥ e`.

  This is exactly the bijectivity of `colim_e Hom(B, T(n)_e) → (colim_e Hom(B, T(0)_e))^{n+1}`
  (`vertices_bijective`); for `B` without property `P` both sides are empty, so the condition
  holds automatically there.  It is what a coproduct description `D(n) = D ⊗ ⋯ ⊗ D` of the
  members of the tower gives, level by level.

`quasiIso_augmentationMap_of_forall` states the result with `𝒜` chosen so that the hypotheses
become: the sieve of morphisms into a `P`-object whose source maps to some `T(0)_e` covers, and
the pro-product condition holds at every object.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.ProCech.sectionSystem`, `Stacks.ProCech.cosimplicialSections`,
  `Stacks.ProCech.sectionsComplex`: the Čech complex `lim_e F(T(0)_e) ⟶ lim_e F(T(1)_e) ⟶ ⋯`.
  They copy `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite.sectionSystem`,
  `...cosimplicialSections` and `...sectionsComplex` word for word, so that on the small
  crystalline site the two agree by `rfl`.
* `Stacks.ProCech.LevelHom`, `Stacks.ProCech.ProHom`: morphisms `B ⟶ T(n)_e` and their classes
  in `colim_e Hom(B, T(n)_e)`; `Stacks.ProCech.vertices` the vertex map.
* `Stacks.ProCech.IsProProductAt`: the pro-product condition.
* `Stacks.ProCech.sectionsOver`: `Γ_P(F) = lim (P.ι.op ⋙ F)`.
* `Stacks.ProCech.augmentation`, `Stacks.ProCech.augmentationMap`: the augmentation, as a
  morphism of groups and as a morphism from the complex `Γ_P(F)[0]`.
* `Stacks.ProCech.cofree`: the presheaf `W ↦ ∏_{B ∈ 𝒜} ∏_{B ⟶ W} H(B)`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.ProCech.mono_augmentation` and `Stacks.ProCech.augmentation_exact`: for every abelian
  sheaf `H` (injective or not), `0 ⟶ Γ_P(H) ⟶ lim_e H(T(0)_e) ⟶ lim_e H(T(1)_e)` is exact.
* `Stacks.ProCech.isZero_homology_sectionsComplex`: for an injective abelian sheaf, the Čech
  complex has zero homology in every degree `n ≥ 1`.
* `Stacks.ProCech.quasiIso_augmentationMap`: the two together, as the statement that
  `Γ_P(H)[0] ⟶ sectionsComplex T H` is a quasi-isomorphism.

## Proof

Degree zero only uses the sheaf property: a cocycle `x` has the same value along any two maps
from an `𝒜`-object to `(T(0)_e)_e` (the two maps come from one map to `(T(1)_e)_e`), hence, by
separatedness, along any two maps from any object; these values glue on the covering sieve of
the objects mapping to `(T(0)_e)_e`.

In positive degrees, an injective abelian sheaf is an injective presheaf
(`CategoryTheory.Sheaf.injective_obj`), and it embeds in the cofree presheaf
`W ↦ ∏_{B ∈ 𝒜} ∏_{B ⟶ W} H(B)` because the `𝒜`-objects cover; so it is a retract of it, and
its Čech complex is a retract of that of the cofree presheaf.  The latter is, by the
pro-product condition, the product over `B ∈ 𝒜` of the cochain complexes of maps from the Čech
nerve of the set `S = colim_e Hom(B, T(0)_e)` to `H(B)`, and these are contracted in positive
degrees by evaluating at a tuple with a fixed point of `S` prepended (`cofree_exists_d_eq`).
No free abelian sheaves and no sheafification of complexes are needed.

## Universes

The site is `C : Type u` with morphisms in `Type v`, and the coefficients are
`AddCommGrpCat.{max u v}`, the universe in which the cofree presheaf (a product over the
objects of `C`) and the limit over `P` live.  For the small crystalline site, with objects in
`Type (u + 1)`, morphisms in `Type u` and coefficients `AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}`, this is the
case `max (u + 1) u = u + 1`.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe w v u

open CategoryTheory Limits Opposite Simplicial

noncomputable section

namespace Stacks.ProCech

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C]

/-! ### The Čech complex along a simplicial system of towers -/

section Complex

variable (T : SimplicialObject (ℕ ⥤ C)) (F : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{w})

/-- The inverse systems `e ↦ F(T(n)_e)` of sections of a presheaf `F` over the levels of the
`n`-th member of a simplicial system of towers `T`, as a functor of `n`. -/
def sectionSystem : SimplexCategory ⥤ (ℕᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{w}) where
  obj n := (T.obj (op n)).op ⋙ F
  map φ := Functor.whiskerRight (NatTrans.op (T.map φ.op)) F
  map_id n := by ext e; simp
  map_comp φ ψ := by ext e; simp

/-- The cosimplicial abelian group `n ↦ lim_e F(T(n)_e)`. -/
def cosimplicialSections : CosimplicialObject AddCommGrpCat.{w} :=
  sectionSystem T F ⋙ lim

/-- The Čech complex `lim_e F(T(0)_e) ⟶ lim_e F(T(1)_e) ⟶ ⋯` of a presheaf `F` along `T`: the
alternating coface map complex of `cosimplicialSections T F`. -/
def sectionsComplex : CochainComplex AddCommGrpCat.{w} ℕ :=
  (AlgebraicTopology.alternatingCofaceMapComplex AddCommGrpCat.{w}).obj
    (cosimplicialSections T F)

/-- The differential of the Čech complex is the alternating sum of the coface maps. -/
lemma sectionsComplex_d (n : ℕ) :
    (sectionsComplex T F).d n (n + 1) =
      ∑ i : Fin (n + 2), (-1 : ℤ) ^ (i : ℕ) •
        ((cosimplicialSections T F).δ i :
          (sectionsComplex T F).X n ⟶ (sectionsComplex T F).X (n + 1)) :=
  CochainComplex.of_d _
    (AlgebraicTopology.AlternatingCofaceMapComplex.objD (cosimplicialSections T F)) n

/-- The projection of the degree-`n` term `lim_e F(T(n)_e)` of the Čech complex onto
`F(T(n)_e)`. -/
def sectionsπ (n e : ℕ) :
    (sectionsComplex T F).X n ⟶ F.obj (op ((T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).obj e)) :=
  limit.π ((T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).op ⋙ F) (op e)

/-- The projections of the degree-`n` term of the Čech complex are compatible with the
transition maps of the tower. -/
@[reassoc]
lemma sectionsπ_w (n : ℕ) {e e' : ℕ} (h : e ≤ e') :
    sectionsπ T F n e' ≫ F.map ((T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).map (homOfLE h)).op = sectionsπ T F n e :=
  limit.w ((T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).op ⋙ F) (homOfLE h).op

/-- The differential of the Čech complex followed by a projection. -/
@[reassoc]
lemma d_comp_sectionsπ (n e : ℕ) :
    (sectionsComplex T F).d n (n + 1) ≫ sectionsπ T F (n + 1) e =
      ∑ i : Fin (n + 2), (-1 : ℤ) ^ (i : ℕ) •
        (sectionsπ T F n e ≫ F.map ((T.map (SimplexCategory.δ i).op).app e).op) := by
  have h (i : Fin (n + 2)) : ((cosimplicialSections T F).δ i :
      (sectionsComplex T F).X n ⟶ (sectionsComplex T F).X (n + 1)) ≫ sectionsπ T F (n + 1) e =
        sectionsπ T F n e ≫ F.map ((T.map (SimplexCategory.δ i).op).app e).op :=
    limMap_π _ _
  rw [sectionsComplex_d]
  refine (Preadditive.sum_comp _ _ _).trans (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_)
  exact (Preadditive.zsmul_comp _ _ _).trans (congrArg _ (h i))

/-- Morphisms into a term of the Čech complex are determined by their projections. -/
lemma sectionsComplex_hom_ext {n : ℕ} {A : AddCommGrpCat.{w}} {f g : A ⟶ (sectionsComplex T F).X n}
    (h : ∀ e, f ≫ sectionsπ T F n e = g ≫ sectionsπ T F n e) : f = g :=
  limit.hom_ext fun e => h e.unop

/-- Elements of a term of the Čech complex are determined by their projections. -/
lemma sectionsComplex_ext {n : ℕ} {x y : (sectionsComplex T F).X n}
    (h : ∀ e, sectionsπ T F n e x = sectionsπ T F n e y) : x = y :=
  Concrete.limit_ext ((T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).op ⋙ F) x y fun e => h e.unop

/-- **Elements of a term of the Čech complex** are the compatible families of sections over the
members of the tower. -/
lemma sectionsComplex_exists_mk {n : ℕ} (s : ∀ e, F.obj (op ((T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).obj e)))
    (hs : ∀ (e e' : ℕ) (h : e ≤ e'), F.map ((T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).map (homOfLE h)).op (s e') = s e) :
    ∃ x : (sectionsComplex T F).X n, ∀ e, sectionsπ T F n e x = s e := by
  let G := (T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).op ⋙ F
  let hl := isLimitOfPreserves (forget AddCommGrpCat.{w}) (limit.isLimit G)
  let σ : (G ⋙ forget AddCommGrpCat.{w}).sections :=
    ⟨fun e => s e.unop, fun {e e'} g => hs e'.unop e.unop (leOfHom g.unop)⟩
  exact ⟨(Types.isLimitEquivSections hl).symm σ, fun e =>
    Types.isLimitEquivSections_symm_apply hl σ (op e)⟩


variable {F} {G K : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{w}}

/-- The degree-`n` component of the map of Čech complexes induced by a morphism of
presheaves. -/
def sectionsMap (α : F ⟶ G) (n : ℕ) :
    (sectionsComplex T F).X n ⟶ (sectionsComplex T G).X n :=
  limMap (Functor.whiskerLeft (T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).op α)

/-- The map of Čech complexes induced by a morphism of presheaves, followed by a projection. -/
@[reassoc]
lemma sectionsMap_π (α : F ⟶ G) (n e : ℕ) :
    sectionsMap T α n ≫ sectionsπ T G n e =
      sectionsπ T F n e ≫ α.app (op ((T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).obj e)) :=
  limMap_π _ _

/-- The map of Čech complexes induced by a morphism of presheaves commutes with the
differentials. -/
lemma sectionsMap_d (α : F ⟶ G) (n : ℕ) :
    sectionsMap T α n ≫ (sectionsComplex T G).d n (n + 1) =
      (sectionsComplex T F).d n (n + 1) ≫ sectionsMap T α (n + 1) := by
  refine sectionsComplex_hom_ext T G fun e => ?_
  simp only [Category.assoc, d_comp_sectionsπ, sectionsMap_π, d_comp_sectionsπ_assoc,
    Preadditive.comp_sum, Preadditive.sum_comp, Preadditive.comp_zsmul,
    Preadditive.zsmul_comp, sectionsMap_π_assoc, NatTrans.naturality]

/-- The map of Čech complexes is compatible with composition. -/
lemma sectionsMap_comp (α : F ⟶ G) (β : G ⟶ K) (n : ℕ) :
    sectionsMap T α n ≫ sectionsMap T β n = sectionsMap T (α ≫ β) n :=
  sectionsComplex_hom_ext T K fun e => by
    simp only [Category.assoc, sectionsMap_π, sectionsMap_π_assoc, NatTrans.comp_app]

/-- The map of Čech complexes induced by the identity is the identity. -/
lemma sectionsMap_id (n : ℕ) : sectionsMap T (𝟙 F) n = 𝟙 _ :=
  sectionsComplex_hom_ext T F fun e => by
    simp only [sectionsMap_π, NatTrans.id_app, Category.comp_id, Category.id_comp]

end Complex

/-! ### Level maps into a tower, and maps into the pro-object -/

section ProHom

variable (T : SimplicialObject (ℕ ⥤ C))

/-- A *level map* from `B` to the `n`-th tower of `T`: a level `e` and a morphism
`B ⟶ T(n)_e`. -/
structure LevelHom (n : ℕ) (B : C) : Type v where
  /-- The level. -/
  level : ℕ
  /-- The morphism into the tower at that level. -/
  hom : B ⟶ (T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).obj level

variable {T}

/-- Composing two transition maps of a tower gives the transition map. -/
lemma map_homOfLE_comp (n : ℕ) {a b c : ℕ} (h₁ : a ≤ b) (h₂ : b ≤ c) :
    (T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).map (homOfLE h₁) ≫ (T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).map (homOfLE h₂) =
      (T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).map (homOfLE (h₁.trans h₂)) := by
  rw [← Functor.map_comp, homOfLE_comp]

namespace LevelHom

variable {n : ℕ} {B : C}

/-- Pushing a level map to a higher level along the transition maps of the tower. -/
def lift (p : LevelHom T n B) {e : ℕ} (h : p.level ≤ e) : LevelHom T n B :=
  ⟨e, p.hom ≫ (T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).map (homOfLE h)⟩

/-- Two level maps are *equivalent* if they agree after pushing both to a common level. -/
def Rel (p q : LevelHom T n B) : Prop :=
  ∃ (e : ℕ) (hp : p.level ≤ e) (hq : q.level ≤ e),
    p.hom ≫ (T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).map (homOfLE hp) = q.hom ≫ (T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).map (homOfLE hq)

/-- The relation `LevelHom.Rel` is reflexive. -/
lemma Rel.refl (p : LevelHom T n B) : Rel p p := ⟨p.level, le_rfl, le_rfl, rfl⟩

/-- The relation `LevelHom.Rel` is symmetric. -/
lemma Rel.symm {p q : LevelHom T n B} (h : Rel p q) : Rel q p := by
  obtain ⟨e, hp, hq, h⟩ := h
  exact ⟨e, hq, hp, h.symm⟩

/-- The relation `LevelHom.Rel` is transitive. -/
lemma Rel.trans {p q r : LevelHom T n B} (h₁ : Rel p q) (h₂ : Rel q r) : Rel p r := by
  obtain ⟨e₁, hp₁, hq₁, h₁⟩ := h₁
  obtain ⟨e₂, hq₂, hr₂, h₂⟩ := h₂
  refine ⟨max e₁ e₂, hp₁.trans (le_max_left _ _), hr₂.trans (le_max_right _ _), ?_⟩
  calc p.hom ≫ (T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).map (homOfLE (hp₁.trans (le_max_left _ _)))
      = (p.hom ≫ (T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).map (homOfLE hp₁)) ≫
          (T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).map (homOfLE (le_max_left e₁ e₂)) := by
        rw [Category.assoc, map_homOfLE_comp]
    _ = (q.hom ≫ (T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).map (homOfLE hq₂)) ≫
          (T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).map (homOfLE (le_max_right e₁ e₂)) := by
        rw [h₁, Category.assoc, Category.assoc, map_homOfLE_comp, map_homOfLE_comp]
    _ = r.hom ≫ (T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).map (homOfLE (hr₂.trans (le_max_right _ _))) := by
        rw [h₂, Category.assoc, map_homOfLE_comp]

/-- A level map is equivalent to its push to a higher level. -/
lemma rel_lift (p : LevelHom T n B) {e : ℕ} (h : p.level ≤ e) : Rel p (p.lift h) :=
  by
  refine ⟨e, h, le_rfl, ?_⟩
  change p.hom ≫ _ = (p.hom ≫ (T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).map (homOfLE h)) ≫
    (T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).map (homOfLE (le_refl e))
  rw [Category.assoc, map_homOfLE_comp]

/-- The level map `B ⟶ T(m)_e` obtained from a level map `B ⟶ T(n)_e` and a morphism
`θ : ⦋m⦌ ⟶ ⦋n⦌` of the simplex category. -/
def map {m : ℕ} (θ : ⦋m⦌ ⟶ ⦋n⦌) (p : LevelHom T n B) : LevelHom T m B :=
  ⟨p.level, p.hom ≫ (T.map θ.op).app p.level⟩

/-- Equivalent level maps stay equivalent under `LevelHom.map`. -/
lemma Rel.map {m : ℕ} (θ : ⦋m⦌ ⟶ ⦋n⦌) {p q : LevelHom T n B} (h : Rel p q) :
    Rel (p.map θ) (q.map θ) := by
  obtain ⟨e, hp, hq, h⟩ := h
  refine ⟨e, hp, hq, ?_⟩
  simp only [LevelHom.map, Category.assoc, ← NatTrans.naturality]
  rw [reassoc_of% h]

/-- Precomposition of a level map with a morphism `Z ⟶ B`. -/
def precomp {Z : C} (a : Z ⟶ B) (p : LevelHom T n B) : LevelHom T n Z :=
  ⟨p.level, a ≫ p.hom⟩

/-- Equivalent level maps stay equivalent under precomposition. -/
lemma Rel.precomp {Z : C} (a : Z ⟶ B) {p q : LevelHom T n B} (h : Rel p q) :
    Rel (p.precomp a) (q.precomp a) := by
  obtain ⟨e, hp, hq, h⟩ := h
  exact ⟨e, hp, hq, by simp [LevelHom.precomp, h]⟩

end LevelHom

variable (T) in
/-- The setoid of level maps up to `LevelHom.Rel`. -/
def levelSetoid (n : ℕ) (B : C) : Setoid (LevelHom T n B) where
  r := LevelHom.Rel
  iseqv := ⟨LevelHom.Rel.refl, LevelHom.Rel.symm, LevelHom.Rel.trans⟩

variable (T) in
/-- The maps from `B` to the pro-object `(T(n)_e)_e`, that is, the colimit over `e` of the sets
of morphisms `B ⟶ T(n)_e`: level maps up to pushing to a common level. -/
def ProHom (n : ℕ) (B : C) : Type v := Quotient (levelSetoid T n B)

namespace ProHom

variable {n : ℕ} {B : C}

/-- The map to the pro-object represented by a level map. -/
def mk (p : LevelHom T n B) : ProHom T n B := Quotient.mk _ p

/-- Every map to the pro-object is represented by a level map. -/
lemma mk_surjective (c : ProHom T n B) : ∃ p : LevelHom T n B, mk p = c :=
  Quotient.exists_rep c

/-- Two level maps represent the same map to the pro-object if and only if they agree after
pushing both to a common level. -/
lemma mk_eq_mk_iff (p q : LevelHom T n B) : mk p = mk q ↔ LevelHom.Rel p q :=
  Quotient.eq (r := levelSetoid T n B)

/-- The map `B ⟶ (T(m)_e)_e` induced by a map `B ⟶ (T(n)_e)_e` and a morphism
`θ : ⦋m⦌ ⟶ ⦋n⦌` of the simplex category. -/
def map {m : ℕ} (θ : ⦋m⦌ ⟶ ⦋n⦌) (c : ProHom T n B) : ProHom T m B :=
  Quotient.map (LevelHom.map θ) (fun _ _ (h : LevelHom.Rel _ _) => h.map θ) c

/-- `ProHom.map` on a representative. -/
lemma map_mk {m : ℕ} (θ : ⦋m⦌ ⟶ ⦋n⦌) (p : LevelHom T n B) : (mk p).map θ = mk (p.map θ) :=
  rfl

/-- `ProHom.map` is functorial. -/
lemma map_map {m k : ℕ} (θ : ⦋m⦌ ⟶ ⦋n⦌) (θ' : ⦋k⦌ ⟶ ⦋m⦌) (c : ProHom T n B) :
    (c.map θ).map θ' = c.map (θ' ≫ θ) := by
  obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := mk_surjective c
  simp only [map_mk]
  congr 1
  simp [LevelHom.map]

/-- `ProHom.map` along an identity is the identity. -/
lemma map_id (c : ProHom T n B) : c.map (𝟙 _) = c := by
  obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := mk_surjective c
  simp only [map_mk]
  congr 1
  simp [LevelHom.map]

/-- Precomposition of a map to the pro-object with a morphism `Z ⟶ B`. -/
def precomp {Z : C} (a : Z ⟶ B) (c : ProHom T n B) : ProHom T n Z :=
  Quotient.map (LevelHom.precomp a) (fun _ _ (h : LevelHom.Rel _ _) => h.precomp a) c

/-- `ProHom.precomp` on a representative. -/
lemma precomp_mk {Z : C} (a : Z ⟶ B) (p : LevelHom T n B) :
    (mk p).precomp a = mk (p.precomp a) :=
  rfl

/-- `ProHom.precomp` is compatible with composition. -/
lemma precomp_comp {Y Z : C} (a : Y ⟶ Z) (b : Z ⟶ B) (c : ProHom T n B) :
    c.precomp (a ≫ b) = (c.precomp b).precomp a := by
  obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := mk_surjective c
  simp only [precomp_mk]
  congr 1
  simp [LevelHom.precomp]

end ProHom

variable (T) in
/-- The `n + 1` vertices `B ⟶ (T(0)_e)_e` of a map `B ⟶ (T(n)_e)_e`, obtained along the
vertex maps `⦋0⦌ ⟶ ⦋n⦌`. -/
def vertices (n : ℕ) (B : C) (c : ProHom T n B) (i : Fin (n + 1)) : ProHom T 0 B :=
  c.map (SimplexCategory.const ⦋0⦌ ⦋n⦌ i)

/-- The vertices of the image of a map under `θ : ⦋m⦌ ⟶ ⦋n⦌` are vertices of the map. -/
lemma vertices_map {m n : ℕ} {B : C} (θ : ⦋m⦌ ⟶ ⦋n⦌) (c : ProHom T n B) (j : Fin (m + 1)) :
    vertices T m B (c.map θ) j = vertices T n B c (θ.toOrderHom j) := by
  rw [vertices, ProHom.map_map, SimplexCategory.const_comp]
  rfl

/-- A map to the pro-object `(T(0)_e)_e` is its own unique vertex. -/
lemma vertices_zero {B : C} (c : ProHom T 0 B) : vertices T 0 B c 0 = c := by
  rw [vertices, SimplexCategory.const_eq_id, ProHom.map_id]

end ProHom

/-! ### The pro-product hypothesis -/

section ProProduct

variable (T : SimplicialObject (ℕ ⥤ C))

/-- **The pro-product condition at an object `B`**: maps from `B` to the pro-object
`(T(n)_e)_e` are the same as `(n + 1)`-tuples of maps from `B` to `(T(0)_e)_e`, through the
`n + 1` vertex maps `⦋0⦌ ⟶ ⦋n⦌`.  Concretely:

* `exists_hom`: for every level `e` and every family `φ i : B ⟶ T(0)_e`, `i : Fin (n + 1)`,
  there is a higher level `e'` and a morphism `ψ : B ⟶ T(n)_{e'}` whose `i`-th vertex is `φ i`
  pushed to the level `e'`;
* `eventually_eq`: two morphisms `ψ ψ' : B ⟶ T(n)_e` with the same vertices agree after pushing
  both to some higher level.

This is the bijectivity of `colim_e Hom(B, T(n)_e) → (colim_e Hom(B, T(0)_e))^{n + 1}`, see
`vertices_bijective`. -/
structure IsProProductAt (B : C) : Prop where
  exists_hom (n e : ℕ) (φ : Fin (n + 1) → (B ⟶ (T.obj (op ⦋0⦌)).obj e)) :
    ∃ (e' : ℕ) (h : e ≤ e') (ψ : B ⟶ (T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).obj e'), ∀ i,
      ψ ≫ (T.map (SimplexCategory.const ⦋0⦌ ⦋n⦌ i).op).app e' =
        φ i ≫ (T.obj (op ⦋0⦌)).map (homOfLE h)
  eventually_eq (n e : ℕ) (ψ ψ' : B ⟶ (T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).obj e)
    (h : ∀ i, ψ ≫ (T.map (SimplexCategory.const ⦋0⦌ ⦋n⦌ i).op).app e =
      ψ' ≫ (T.map (SimplexCategory.const ⦋0⦌ ⦋n⦌ i).op).app e) :
    ∃ (e' : ℕ) (h' : e ≤ e'),
      ψ ≫ (T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).map (homOfLE h') = ψ' ≫ (T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).map (homOfLE h')

variable {T}

/-- Finitely many maps to a pro-object are represented by level maps at one common level. -/
lemma ProHom.exists_level {ι : Type*} [Finite ι] {n : ℕ} {B : C} (c : ι → ProHom T n B) :
    ∃ (e : ℕ) (φ : ι → (B ⟶ (T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).obj e)), ∀ i, c i = ProHom.mk ⟨e, φ i⟩ := by
  choose p hp using fun i => ProHom.mk_surjective (c i)
  obtain ⟨E, hE⟩ := Finite.exists_le (fun i => (p i).level)
  refine ⟨E, fun i => ((p i).lift (hE i)).hom, fun i => ?_⟩
  rw [← hp i, ProHom.mk_eq_mk_iff]
  exact LevelHom.rel_lift _ _

/-- If finitely many pairs of level maps at one level represent the same maps to the
pro-object, then they agree after pushing to one common higher level. -/
lemma ProHom.exists_eq_of_mk_eq {ι : Type*} [Finite ι] {n e : ℕ} {B : C}
    (φ ψ : ι → (B ⟶ (T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).obj e))
    (h : ∀ i, ProHom.mk ⟨e, φ i⟩ = ProHom.mk ⟨e, ψ i⟩) :
    ∃ (E : ℕ) (hE : e ≤ E), ∀ i,
      φ i ≫ (T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).map (homOfLE hE) = ψ i ≫ (T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).map (homOfLE hE) := by
  choose f hf hf' hφψ using fun i => (ProHom.mk_eq_mk_iff _ _).1 (h i)
  obtain ⟨E, hE⟩ := Finite.exists_le f
  refine ⟨max E e, le_max_right _ _, fun i => ?_⟩
  have h₁ : f i ≤ max E e := (hE i).trans (le_max_left _ _)
  simpa only [Category.assoc, map_homOfLE_comp] using
    congrArg (· ≫ (T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).map (homOfLE h₁)) (hφψ i)

/-- The vertices of a map represented by a level map. -/
lemma vertices_mk {n : ℕ} {B : C} (p : LevelHom T n B) (i : Fin (n + 1)) :
    vertices T n B (ProHom.mk p) i =
      ProHom.mk ⟨p.level, p.hom ≫ (T.map (SimplexCategory.const ⦋0⦌ ⦋n⦌ i).op).app p.level⟩ :=
  rfl

/-- At an object satisfying the pro-product condition, a map to `(T(n)_e)_e` is determined by
its vertices. -/
private lemma vertices_injective {B : C} (hB : IsProProductAt T B) (n : ℕ) :
    Function.Injective (vertices T n B) := by
  intro c c' hcc'
  obtain ⟨e, φ, hφ⟩ := ProHom.exists_level ![c, c']
  have h0 : c = ProHom.mk ⟨e, φ 0⟩ := hφ 0
  have h1 : c' = ProHom.mk ⟨e, φ 1⟩ := hφ 1
  subst h0 h1
  obtain ⟨E, hE, hv⟩ := ProHom.exists_eq_of_mk_eq
    (fun i => φ 0 ≫ (T.map (SimplexCategory.const ⦋0⦌ ⦋n⦌ i).op).app e)
    (fun i => φ 1 ≫ (T.map (SimplexCategory.const ⦋0⦌ ⦋n⦌ i).op).app e)
    (fun i => congrFun hcc' i)
  obtain ⟨E', hE', hφ'⟩ := hB.eventually_eq n E (φ 0 ≫ (T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).map (homOfLE hE))
    (φ 1 ≫ (T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).map (homOfLE hE))
    (fun i => by simpa only [Category.assoc, NatTrans.naturality] using hv i)
  rw [ProHom.mk_eq_mk_iff]
  refine ⟨E', hE.trans hE', hE.trans hE', ?_⟩
  simpa only [Category.assoc, map_homOfLE_comp] using hφ'

/-- At an object satisfying the pro-product condition, every tuple of maps to `(T(0)_e)_e` is
the vertex tuple of a map to `(T(n)_e)_e`. -/
private lemma vertices_surjective {B : C} (hB : IsProProductAt T B) (n : ℕ) :
    Function.Surjective (vertices T n B) := by
  intro f
  obtain ⟨e, φ, hφ⟩ := ProHom.exists_level f
  obtain ⟨e', h, ψ, hψ⟩ := hB.exists_hom n e φ
  refine ⟨ProHom.mk ⟨e', ψ⟩, funext fun i => ?_⟩
  rw [vertices_mk, hφ i, ProHom.mk_eq_mk_iff]
  dsimp only
  rw [hψ i]
  exact (LevelHom.rel_lift ⟨e, φ i⟩ h).symm

/-- **Maps into `(T(n)_e)_e` are tuples of maps into `(T(0)_e)_e`** at an object satisfying the
pro-product condition: the vertex map is bijective. -/
lemma vertices_bijective {B : C} (hB : IsProProductAt T B) (n : ℕ) :
    Function.Bijective (vertices T n B) :=
  ⟨vertices_injective hB n, vertices_surjective hB n⟩

end ProProduct

/-! ### Evaluating a section of the Čech complex at a map to the pro-object -/

section Eval

variable {T : SimplicialObject (ℕ ⥤ C)} (F : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{w})

/-- The value at `B` of an element of `lim_e F(T(n)_e)` along a level map `B ⟶ T(n)_e`. -/
def LevelHom.eval {n : ℕ} {B : C} (p : LevelHom T n B) :
    (sectionsComplex T F).X n ⟶ F.obj (op B) :=
  sectionsπ T F n p.level ≫ F.map p.hom.op

/-- Pushing a level map to a higher level does not change the value along it. -/
lemma LevelHom.eval_lift {n : ℕ} {B : C} (p : LevelHom T n B) {e : ℕ} (h : p.level ≤ e) :
    (p.lift h).eval F = p.eval F := by
  simp only [LevelHom.eval, LevelHom.lift, op_comp, F.map_comp]
  rw [sectionsπ_w_assoc]

/-- Equivalent level maps give the same values. -/
lemma LevelHom.eval_eq_of_rel {n : ℕ} {B : C} {p q : LevelHom T n B} (h : LevelHom.Rel p q) :
    p.eval F = q.eval F := by
  obtain ⟨e, hp, hq, h⟩ := h
  rw [← p.eval_lift F hp, ← q.eval_lift F hq]
  simp only [LevelHom.lift, h]

/-- The value at `B` of an element of `lim_e F(T(n)_e)` along a map `B ⟶ (T(n)_e)_e` to the
pro-object. -/
def ProHom.eval {n : ℕ} {B : C} (c : ProHom T n B) :
    (sectionsComplex T F).X n ⟶ F.obj (op B) :=
  Quotient.lift (LevelHom.eval F) (fun _ _ (h : LevelHom.Rel _ _) => LevelHom.eval_eq_of_rel F h) c

/-- `ProHom.eval` on a representative. -/
lemma ProHom.eval_mk {n : ℕ} {B : C} (p : LevelHom T n B) :
    (ProHom.mk p).eval F = p.eval F :=
  rfl

/-- Evaluating along the identity of a member of the tower is the projection. -/
lemma ProHom.eval_mk_id (n e : ℕ) :
    (ProHom.mk (⟨e, 𝟙 _⟩ : LevelHom T n _)).eval F = sectionsπ T F n e := by
  simp [ProHom.eval_mk, LevelHom.eval]

/-- Evaluating along a precomposed map is restricting the value. -/
lemma ProHom.precomp_eval {n : ℕ} {B Z : C} (a : Z ⟶ B) (c : ProHom T n B) :
    (c.precomp a).eval F = c.eval F ≫ F.map a.op := by
  obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := ProHom.mk_surjective c
  simp [ProHom.eval_mk, ProHom.precomp_mk, LevelHom.eval, LevelHom.precomp]

/-- The differential of the Čech complex, evaluated along a map to the pro-object. -/
lemma ProHom.d_comp_eval {n : ℕ} {B : C} (c : ProHom T (n + 1) B) :
    (sectionsComplex T F).d n (n + 1) ≫ c.eval F =
      ∑ i : Fin (n + 2), (-1 : ℤ) ^ (i : ℕ) • (c.map (SimplexCategory.δ i)).eval F := by
  obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := ProHom.mk_surjective c
  simp only [ProHom.eval_mk, ProHom.map_mk, LevelHom.eval, LevelHom.map]
  rw [← Category.assoc, d_comp_sectionsπ, Preadditive.sum_comp]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
  simp

end Eval

/-! ### The cofree presheaf on the values at a family of objects -/

section Cofree

/-- A finite sum of integer multiples of morphisms of abelian groups, applied to an element. -/
lemma sum_zsmul_apply {M N : AddCommGrpCat.{w}} {ι : Type*} (s : Finset ι) (c : ι → ℤ)
    (f : ι → (M ⟶ N)) (x : M) : (∑ i ∈ s, c i • f i) x = ∑ i ∈ s, c i • f i x := by
  classical
  induction s using Finset.induction_on with
  | empty => simp
  | insert a s ha ih =>
    rw [Finset.sum_insert ha, Finset.sum_insert ha, AddCommGrpCat.hom_add_apply, ih]
    simp

/-- The value of a face map `δ i : ⦋n⦌ ⟶ ⦋n + 1⦌` at `j` is `i.succAbove j`. -/
lemma δ_toOrderHom_apply {n : ℕ} (i : Fin (n + 2)) (j : Fin (n + 1)) :
    (SimplexCategory.δ i).toOrderHom j = i.succAbove j :=
  rfl

/-- At an object satisfying the pro-product condition, the `i`-th face of a map to
`(T(n + 1)_e)_e` is the map to `(T(n)_e)_e` whose vertices are the corresponding vertices. -/
private lemma map_δ_eq_of_vertices {T : SimplicialObject (ℕ ⥤ C)} {B : C}
    (hB : IsProProductAt T B) {n : ℕ} (k : ProHom T (n + 1) B) (c : ProHom T n B)
    (i : Fin (n + 2))
    (h : ∀ j, vertices T (n + 1) B k (i.succAbove j) = vertices T n B c j) :
    k.map (SimplexCategory.δ i) = c :=
  vertices_injective hB n (funext fun j => by rw [vertices_map, δ_toOrderHom_apply, h])

variable (𝒜 : ObjectProperty C) (H : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{max u v})

/-- The *cofree presheaf* on the values of `H` at the objects with property `𝒜`:
`W ↦ ∏_{B ∈ 𝒜} ∏_{B ⟶ W} H(B)`. -/
def cofree : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{max u v} where
  obj W := AddCommGrpCat.of ((B : 𝒜.FullSubcategory) → (B.obj ⟶ W.unop) → H.obj (op B.obj))
  map g := AddCommGrpCat.ofHom
    { toFun := fun s B f => s B (f ≫ g.unop)
      map_zero' := rfl
      map_add' := fun _ _ => rfl }
  map_id W := AddCommGrpCat.ext fun s => funext fun B => funext fun f => by simp
  map_comp g g' := AddCommGrpCat.ext fun s => funext fun B => funext fun f => by simp

/-- The canonical morphism `H ⟶ cofree 𝒜 H`, sending a section to its restrictions. -/
def cofreeι : H ⟶ cofree 𝒜 H where
  app W := AddCommGrpCat.ofHom
    { toFun := fun s B f => H.map f.op s
      map_zero' := funext fun B => funext fun f => by simp
      map_add' := fun s s' => funext fun B => funext fun f => by simp }
  naturality W W' g := AddCommGrpCat.ext fun s => funext fun B => funext fun f => by
    change H.map f.op (H.map g s) = H.map (f ≫ g.unop).op s
    rw [op_comp, Quiver.Hom.op_unop, H.map_comp, ConcreteCategory.comp_apply]

/-- The component at `B ∈ 𝒜` along the identity, `cofree 𝒜 H (B) ⟶ H(B)`. -/
def cofreeEval (B : 𝒜.FullSubcategory) : (cofree 𝒜 H).obj (op B.obj) ⟶ H.obj (op B.obj) :=
  AddCommGrpCat.ofHom
    { toFun := fun s => s B (𝟙 _)
      map_zero' := rfl
      map_add' := fun _ _ => rfl }

variable {T : SimplicialObject (ℕ ⥤ C)}

/-- The value at `B ∈ 𝒜` of an element of the Čech complex of the cofree presheaf along a map
`B ⟶ (T(n)_e)_e`. -/
def cofreeValue {n : ℕ} (B : 𝒜.FullSubcategory) (c : ProHom T n B.obj) :
    (sectionsComplex T (cofree 𝒜 H)).X n ⟶ H.obj (op B.obj) :=
  c.eval (cofree 𝒜 H) ≫ cofreeEval 𝒜 H B

/-- `cofreeValue` along a level map. -/
lemma cofreeValue_mk {n : ℕ} (B : 𝒜.FullSubcategory) (p : LevelHom T n B.obj)
    (x : (sectionsComplex T (cofree 𝒜 H)).X n) :
    cofreeValue 𝒜 H B (ProHom.mk p) x = sectionsπ T (cofree 𝒜 H) n p.level x B p.hom := by
  change sectionsπ T (cofree 𝒜 H) n p.level x B (𝟙 _ ≫ p.hom) = _
  rw [Category.id_comp]

/-- `cofreeValue` after the differential. -/
lemma cofreeValue_d {n : ℕ} (B : 𝒜.FullSubcategory) (c : ProHom T (n + 1) B.obj)
    (z : (sectionsComplex T (cofree 𝒜 H)).X n) :
    cofreeValue 𝒜 H B c ((sectionsComplex T (cofree 𝒜 H)).d n (n + 1) z) =
      ∑ i : Fin (n + 2), (-1 : ℤ) ^ (i : ℕ) •
        cofreeValue 𝒜 H B (c.map (SimplexCategory.δ i)) z := by
  have h := congrArg (· ≫ cofreeEval 𝒜 H B) (ProHom.d_comp_eval (cofree 𝒜 H) c)
  simp only [Category.assoc, Preadditive.sum_comp, Preadditive.zsmul_comp] at h
  have h' := ConcreteCategory.congr_hom h z
  rw [sum_zsmul_apply] at h'
  exact h'

/-- Elements of the Čech complex of the cofree presheaf are determined by their values. -/
lemma cofree_ext {n : ℕ} {x y : (sectionsComplex T (cofree 𝒜 H)).X n}
    (h : ∀ (B : 𝒜.FullSubcategory) (c : ProHom T n B.obj),
      cofreeValue 𝒜 H B c x = cofreeValue 𝒜 H B c y) : x = y := by
  refine sectionsComplex_ext T _ fun e => funext fun B => funext fun f => ?_
  have := h B (ProHom.mk ⟨e, f⟩)
  rwa [cofreeValue_mk, cofreeValue_mk] at this

/-- **Elements of the Čech complex of the cofree presheaf** are the families of values along
the maps to the pro-object. -/
lemma cofree_exists_mk {n : ℕ}
    (Y : ∀ B : 𝒜.FullSubcategory, ProHom T n B.obj → H.obj (op B.obj)) :
    ∃ y : (sectionsComplex T (cofree 𝒜 H)).X n,
      ∀ (B : 𝒜.FullSubcategory) (c : ProHom T n B.obj), cofreeValue 𝒜 H B c y = Y B c := by
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := sectionsComplex_exists_mk T (cofree 𝒜 H)
    (fun e B f => Y B (ProHom.mk ⟨e, f⟩)) (fun e e' h => funext fun B => funext fun f =>
      congrArg (Y B) ((ProHom.mk_eq_mk_iff _ _).2 (LevelHom.rel_lift ⟨e, f⟩ h)).symm)
  refine ⟨y, fun B c => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := ProHom.mk_surjective c
  rw [cofreeValue_mk, hy]

/-- **The Čech complex of the cofree presheaf is exact in positive degrees** when the objects
with property `𝒜` satisfy the pro-product condition.  The contracting homotopy evaluates a
cochain at the tuple of maps to `(T(0)_e)_e` with a fixed base point prepended. -/
theorem cofree_exists_d_eq (hT : ∀ B : 𝒜.FullSubcategory, IsProProductAt T B.obj) (m : ℕ)
    (x : (sectionsComplex T (cofree 𝒜 H)).X (m + 1))
    (hx : (sectionsComplex T (cofree 𝒜 H)).d (m + 1) (m + 1 + 1) x = 0) :
    ∃ y, (sectionsComplex T (cofree 𝒜 H)).d m (m + 1) y = x := by
  let V (B : 𝒜.FullSubcategory) (n : ℕ) :
      ProHom T n B.obj ≃ (Fin (n + 1) → ProHom T 0 B.obj) :=
    Equiv.ofBijective _ (vertices_bijective (hT B) n)
  let base (B : 𝒜.FullSubcategory) (h : Nonempty (ProHom T 0 B.obj)) : ProHom T 0 B.obj :=
    Classical.choice h
  let Y (B : 𝒜.FullSubcategory) (c : ProHom T m B.obj) : H.obj (op B.obj) :=
    cofreeValue 𝒜 H B ((V B (m + 1)).symm
      (Fin.cons (base B ⟨vertices T m B.obj c 0⟩) (vertices T m B.obj c))) x
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := cofree_exists_mk 𝒜 H Y
  refine ⟨y, cofree_ext 𝒜 H fun B c => ?_⟩
  let b := base B ⟨vertices T (m + 1) B.obj c 0⟩
  let k := (V B (m + 1 + 1)).symm (Fin.cons b (vertices T (m + 1) B.obj c))
  have hkv : vertices T (m + 1 + 1) B.obj k = Fin.cons b (vertices T (m + 1) B.obj c) :=
    (V B (m + 1 + 1)).apply_symm_apply _
  have hk0 : k.map (SimplexCategory.δ 0) = c :=
    map_δ_eq_of_vertices (hT B) k c 0 fun j => by
      rw [hkv, Fin.succAbove_zero, Fin.cons_succ]
  have hks (i : Fin (m + 2)) : k.map (SimplexCategory.δ i.succ) =
      (V B (m + 1)).symm (Fin.cons b (vertices T m B.obj (c.map (SimplexCategory.δ i)))) :=
    map_δ_eq_of_vertices (hT B) k _ i.succ fun j => by
      rw [hkv]
      change _ = V B (m + 1) ((V B (m + 1)).symm _) j
      rw [Equiv.apply_symm_apply]
      refine Fin.cases ?_ (fun j => ?_) j
      · rw [Fin.succ_succAbove_zero, Fin.cons_zero, Fin.cons_zero]
      · rw [Fin.succ_succAbove_succ, Fin.cons_succ, Fin.cons_succ, vertices_map,
          δ_toOrderHom_apply]
  have hx' := congrArg (cofreeValue 𝒜 H B k) hx
  rw [map_zero, cofreeValue_d, Fin.sum_univ_succ, hk0] at hx'
  simp only [hks, Fin.val_zero, pow_zero, one_smul, Fin.val_succ, pow_succ, mul_neg, mul_one,
    neg_smul, Finset.sum_neg_distrib] at hx'
  rw [cofreeValue_d]
  simp only [hy]
  exact (add_neg_eq_zero.mp hx').symm

/-- An abelian presheaf which is separated for the coverings by objects with property `𝒜`
embeds in its cofree presheaf. -/
lemma mono_cofreeι (h : ∀ (W : C) (s : H.obj (op W)),
    (∀ (B : C) (_ : 𝒜 B) (f : B ⟶ W), H.map f.op s = 0) → s = 0) :
    Mono (cofreeι 𝒜 H) := by
  have (W : Cᵒᵖ) : Mono ((cofreeι 𝒜 H).app W) := by
    rw [AddCommGrpCat.mono_iff_injective, injective_iff_map_eq_zero]
    intro s hs
    exact h W.unop s fun B hB f => congrFun (congrFun hs ⟨B, hB⟩) f
  exact NatTrans.mono_of_mono_app _

/-- **The Čech complex of an injective presheaf which embeds in its cofree presheaf is exact
in positive degrees**: it is a retract of the Čech complex of the cofree presheaf. -/
theorem exists_d_eq_of_injective [Injective H] (hmono : Mono (cofreeι 𝒜 H))
    (hT : ∀ B : 𝒜.FullSubcategory, IsProProductAt T B.obj) (m : ℕ)
    (x : (sectionsComplex T H).X (m + 1))
    (hx : (sectionsComplex T H).d (m + 1) (m + 1 + 1) x = 0) :
    ∃ y, (sectionsComplex T H).d m (m + 1) y = x := by
  let r := Injective.factorThru (𝟙 H) (cofreeι 𝒜 H)
  have hr : cofreeι 𝒜 H ≫ r = 𝟙 H := Injective.comp_factorThru _ _
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := cofree_exists_d_eq 𝒜 H hT m (sectionsMap T (cofreeι 𝒜 H) (m + 1) x) (by
      rw [← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, sectionsMap_d, ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, hx,
        map_zero])
  refine ⟨sectionsMap T r m y, ?_⟩
  rw [← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, sectionsMap_d, ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, hy,
    ← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, sectionsMap_comp, hr, sectionsMap_id]
  rfl

end Cofree

/-! ### Sections over `P` and the augmentation -/

section Augmentation

variable (T : SimplicialObject (ℕ ⥤ C)) (P : ObjectProperty C)

/-- **The sections of a presheaf over `P`**: the limit of `F` over the full subcategory of the
objects with property `P`.  When `P` is the property of lying over an open `W`, these are the
sections over `W` of the direct image. -/
abbrev sectionsOver (F : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{max u v}) : AddCommGrpCat.{max u v} :=
  limit (P.ι.op ⋙ F)

/-- The restriction of the sections over `P` to an object `B` with property `P`. -/
def sectionsOverπ (F : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{max u v}) (B : C) (hB : P B) :
    sectionsOver P F ⟶ F.obj (op B) :=
  limit.π (P.ι.op ⋙ F) (op ⟨B, hB⟩)

/-- The restrictions of the sections over `P` are compatible with the restriction maps. -/
@[reassoc]
lemma sectionsOverπ_map (F : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{max u v}) {B' B : C} (g : B' ⟶ B)
    (hB : P B) (hB' : P B') :
    sectionsOverπ P F B hB ≫ F.map g.op = sectionsOverπ P F B' hB' :=
  limit.w (P.ι.op ⋙ F) (ObjectProperty.homMk g : (⟨B', hB'⟩ : P.FullSubcategory) ⟶ ⟨B, hB⟩).op

/-- Sections over `P` are determined by their restrictions. -/
lemma sectionsOver_ext (F : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{max u v}) {x y : sectionsOver P F}
    (h : ∀ (B : C) (hB : P B), sectionsOverπ P F B hB x = sectionsOverπ P F B hB y) : x = y :=
  Concrete.limit_ext _ x y fun j => h j.unop.obj j.unop.property

/-- **Sections over `P`** are the compatible families of sections over the objects with
property `P`. -/
lemma sectionsOver_exists_mk (F : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{max u v}) (s : ∀ B, P B → F.obj (op B))
    (hs : ∀ (B B' : C) (g : B' ⟶ B) (hB : P B) (hB' : P B'), F.map g.op (s B hB) = s B' hB') :
    ∃ y : sectionsOver P F, ∀ (B : C) (hB : P B), sectionsOverπ P F B hB y = s B hB := by
  let G := P.ι.op ⋙ F
  let hl := isLimitOfPreserves (forget AddCommGrpCat.{max u v}) (limit.isLimit G)
  let σ : (G ⋙ forget AddCommGrpCat.{max u v}).sections :=
    ⟨fun j => s j.unop.obj j.unop.property, fun {j j'} f =>
      hs j.unop.obj j'.unop.obj f.unop.hom j.unop.property j'.unop.property⟩
  exact ⟨(Types.isLimitEquivSections hl).symm σ, fun B hB =>
    Types.isLimitEquivSections_symm_apply hl σ (op ⟨B, hB⟩)⟩

variable {T P}

/-- **The augmentation** `Γ_P(F) ⟶ lim_e F(T(0)_e)`, restricting sections over `P` to the
members `T(0)_e` of the tower, which have property `P`. -/
def augmentation (hT : ∀ n e, P ((T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).obj e)) (F : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{max u v}) :
    sectionsOver P F ⟶ (sectionsComplex T F).X 0 :=
  limit.lift ((T.obj (op ⦋0⦌)).op ⋙ F)
    { pt := sectionsOver P F
      π :=
        { app e := sectionsOverπ P F ((T.obj (op ⦋0⦌)).obj e.unop) (hT 0 e.unop)
          naturality _ _ _ :=
            (Category.id_comp _).trans (sectionsOverπ_map P F _ _ _).symm } }

/-- The augmentation followed by a projection. -/
@[reassoc]
lemma augmentation_π (hT : ∀ n e, P ((T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).obj e))
    (F : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{max u v}) (e : ℕ) :
    augmentation hT F ≫ sectionsπ T F 0 e =
      sectionsOverπ P F ((T.obj (op ⦋0⦌)).obj e) (hT 0 e) :=
  limit.lift_π _ _

/-- The augmentation followed by the value along a level map `B ⟶ T(0)_e` is the restriction
of the sections over `P` to `B`. -/
lemma augmentation_eval (hT : ∀ n e, P ((T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).obj e))
    (F : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{max u v}) {B : C} (p : LevelHom T 0 B) (hB : P B) :
    augmentation hT F ≫ (ProHom.mk p).eval F = sectionsOverπ P F B hB := by
  rw [ProHom.eval_mk, LevelHom.eval, augmentation_π_assoc, sectionsOverπ_map]

/-- The augmentation composed with the first differential vanishes. -/
lemma augmentation_comp_d (hT : ∀ n e, P ((T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).obj e))
    (F : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{max u v}) :
    augmentation hT F ≫ (sectionsComplex T F).d 0 1 = 0 := by
  refine sectionsComplex_hom_ext T F fun e => ?_
  rw [Category.assoc, zero_comp]
  change augmentation hT F ≫ (sectionsComplex T F).d 0 (0 + 1) ≫ sectionsπ T F (0 + 1) e = 0
  rw [d_comp_sectionsπ, Preadditive.comp_sum, Fin.sum_univ_two]
  simp only [Preadditive.comp_zsmul]
  have h (i : Fin 2) : augmentation hT F ≫ sectionsπ T F 0 e ≫
      F.map ((T.map (SimplexCategory.δ i).op).app e).op =
        sectionsOverπ P F _ (hT 1 e) :=
    augmentation_eval hT F ⟨e, (T.map (SimplexCategory.δ i).op).app e⟩ (hT 1 e)
  rw [h 0, h 1, Fin.val_zero, Fin.val_one, pow_zero, pow_one, one_smul, neg_one_smul,
    add_neg_cancel]

/-- **The augmentation as a morphism of complexes** from `Γ_P(F)`, placed in degree `0`, to the
Čech complex. -/
def augmentationMap (hT : ∀ n e, P ((T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).obj e))
    (F : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{max u v}) :
    (CochainComplex.single₀ AddCommGrpCat.{max u v}).obj (sectionsOver P F) ⟶
      sectionsComplex T F :=
  (CochainComplex.fromSingle₀Equiv _ _).symm ⟨augmentation hT F, augmentation_comp_d hT F⟩

end Augmentation

/-! ### Sheaves -/

section Sheaf

variable {J : GrothendieckTopology C} (T : SimplicialObject (ℕ ⥤ C)) {P 𝒜 : ObjectProperty C}

/-- The sieve on `W` of the morphisms `Z ⟶ W` whose source admits a map to `(T(0)_e)_e`. -/
def reachSieve (W : C) : Sieve W where
  arrows Z _ := Nonempty (ProHom T 0 Z)
  downward_closed := fun ⟨c⟩ a => ⟨c.precomp a⟩

variable {T}

/-- The sieve `reachSieve T W` covers every object `W` with property `P`. -/
lemma reachSieve_mem (hP : ∀ ⦃B' B : C⦄, (B' ⟶ B) → P B → P B')
    (h𝒜 : ∀ B : C, Sieve.generate (fun (B' : C) (_ : B' ⟶ B) => 𝒜 B') ∈ J B)
    (hT₁ : ∀ B : C, 𝒜 B → P B → ∃ e, Nonempty (B ⟶ (T.obj (op ⦋0⦌)).obj e))
    {W : C} (hW : P W) : reachSieve T W ∈ J W := by
  refine J.superset_covering ?_ (h𝒜 W)
  rintro Z g ⟨B', a, f, hB', -⟩
  obtain ⟨e, ⟨k⟩⟩ := hT₁ B' hB' (hP f hW)
  exact ⟨ProHom.mk ⟨e, a ≫ k⟩⟩

/-- A section of an abelian sheaf vanishing on every object with property `𝒜` over its domain
vanishes, when those objects cover. -/
lemma eq_zero_of_sheaf (H : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{max u v})
    (h𝒜 : ∀ B : C, Sieve.generate (fun (B' : C) (_ : B' ⟶ B) => 𝒜 B') ∈ J B)
    (W : C) (s : H.obj.obj (op W)) (hs : ∀ (B : C) (_ : 𝒜 B) (f : B ⟶ W), H.obj.map f.op s = 0) :
    s = 0 := by
  refine Sheaf.isSeparated H W _ (h𝒜 W) s 0 ?_
  rintro Z g ⟨B', a, f, hB', rfl⟩
  rw [op_comp, Functor.map_comp, ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, hs B' hB' f, map_zero, map_zero]

/-- A cocycle of degree `0` has the same value along any two maps from an object satisfying the
pro-product condition to `(T(0)_e)_e`. -/
lemma eval_eq_of_d_eq_zero (F : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{w}) {B : C} (hB : IsProProductAt T B)
    (x : (sectionsComplex T F).X 0) (hx : (sectionsComplex T F).d 0 1 x = 0)
    (c c' : ProHom T 0 B) : c.eval F x = c'.eval F x := by
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := (vertices_bijective hB 1).2 ![c, c']
  have h1 : k.map (SimplexCategory.δ 1) = c :=
    map_δ_eq_of_vertices hB k c 1 fun j => by
      rw [Fin.fin_one_eq_zero j, vertices_zero]
      exact congrFun hk 0
  have h0 : k.map (SimplexCategory.δ 0) = c' :=
    map_δ_eq_of_vertices hB k c' 0 fun j => by
      rw [Fin.fin_one_eq_zero j, vertices_zero]
      exact congrFun hk 1
  have h := ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (ProHom.d_comp_eval F (n := 0) k) x
  have hx' : (sectionsComplex T F).d 0 (0 + 1) x = 0 := hx
  rw [ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, sum_zsmul_apply, Fin.sum_univ_two, hx', map_zero, h0,
    h1] at h
  simp only [Fin.val_zero, Fin.val_one, pow_zero, pow_one, one_smul, neg_smul] at h
  exact (add_neg_eq_zero.mp h.symm).symm

/-- On an abelian sheaf, a cocycle of degree `0` has the same value along any two maps from any
object to `(T(0)_e)_e`, when the objects satisfying the pro-product condition cover. -/
lemma eval_eq_of_d_eq_zero_of_sheaf (H : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{max u v})
    (h𝒜 : ∀ B : C, Sieve.generate (fun (B' : C) (_ : B' ⟶ B) => 𝒜 B') ∈ J B)
    (hT₂ : ∀ B : C, 𝒜 B → IsProProductAt T B)
    (x : (sectionsComplex T H.obj).X 0) (hx : (sectionsComplex T H.obj).d 0 1 x = 0)
    (Z : C) (c c' : ProHom T 0 Z) : c.eval H.obj x = c'.eval H.obj x := by
  refine Sheaf.isSeparated H Z _ (h𝒜 Z) _ _ ?_
  rintro Y g ⟨B', a, f, hB', rfl⟩
  have h := eval_eq_of_d_eq_zero H.obj (hT₂ B' hB') x hx (c.precomp f) (c'.precomp f)
  rw [ProHom.precomp_eval, ProHom.precomp_eval, ConcreteCategory.comp_apply,
    ConcreteCategory.comp_apply] at h
  rw [op_comp, Functor.map_comp, ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, h]

/-- **The augmentation is injective** for an abelian sheaf. -/
theorem mono_augmentation (H : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{max u v})
    (hP : ∀ ⦃B' B : C⦄, (B' ⟶ B) → P B → P B') (hT : ∀ n e, P ((T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).obj e))
    (h𝒜 : ∀ B : C, Sieve.generate (fun (B' : C) (_ : B' ⟶ B) => 𝒜 B') ∈ J B)
    (hT₁ : ∀ B : C, 𝒜 B → P B → ∃ e, Nonempty (B ⟶ (T.obj (op ⦋0⦌)).obj e)) :
    Mono (augmentation hT H.obj) := by
  rw [AddCommGrpCat.mono_iff_injective, injective_iff_map_eq_zero]
  intro y hy
  refine sectionsOver_ext P H.obj fun W hW => ?_
  rw [map_zero]
  refine Sheaf.isSeparated H W _ (reachSieve_mem hP h𝒜 hT₁ hW) _ 0 ?_
  rintro Z g ⟨c⟩
  obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := ProHom.mk_surjective c
  have hZ : P Z := hP p.hom (hT 0 p.level)
  rw [map_zero, ← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, sectionsOverπ_map P H.obj g hW hZ,
    ← augmentation_eval hT H.obj p hZ, ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, hy, map_zero]

/-- **Exactness of `0 ⟶ Γ_P(H) ⟶ lim_e H(T(0)_e) ⟶ lim_e H(T(1)_e)`** at the middle term, for
an abelian sheaf `H`. -/
theorem augmentation_exact (H : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{max u v})
    (hP : ∀ ⦃B' B : C⦄, (B' ⟶ B) → P B → P B') (hT : ∀ n e, P ((T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).obj e))
    (h𝒜 : ∀ B : C, Sieve.generate (fun (B' : C) (_ : B' ⟶ B) => 𝒜 B') ∈ J B)
    (hT₁ : ∀ B : C, 𝒜 B → P B → ∃ e, Nonempty (B ⟶ (T.obj (op ⦋0⦌)).obj e))
    (hT₂ : ∀ B : C, 𝒜 B → IsProProductAt T B) :
    (ShortComplex.mk (augmentation hT H.obj) ((sectionsComplex T H.obj).d 0 1)
      (augmentation_comp_d hT H.obj)).Exact := by
  rw [ShortComplex.ab_exact_iff]
  intro x hx
  have hW' := eval_eq_of_d_eq_zero_of_sheaf H h𝒜 hT₂ x hx
  have glue (W : P.FullSubcategory) : ∃ t : H.obj.obj (op W.obj), ∀ (Z : C) (g : Z ⟶ W.obj)
      (c : ProHom T 0 Z), H.obj.map g.op t = c.eval H.obj x := by
    have hsh := ((isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type _ _).1
      ((sheafCompose J (forget AddCommGrpCat.{max u v})).obj H).property) (reachSieve T W.obj)
      (reachSieve_mem hP h𝒜 hT₁ W.property)
    let fam : Presieve.FamilyOfElements (H.obj ⋙ forget AddCommGrpCat.{max u v})
        (reachSieve T W.obj).arrows := fun Z _ hg => (Classical.choice hg).eval H.obj x
    have hfam : fam.Compatible := by
      intro Y₁ Y₂ Z g₁ g₂ f₁ f₂ h₁ h₂ _
      change H.obj.map g₁.op ((Classical.choice h₁).eval H.obj x) =
        H.obj.map g₂.op ((Classical.choice h₂).eval H.obj x)
      rw [← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ← ProHom.precomp_eval,
        ← ProHom.precomp_eval]
      exact hW' Z _ _
    obtain ⟨t, ht, -⟩ := hsh fam hfam
    exact ⟨t, fun Z g c => (ht g ⟨c⟩).trans (hW' Z _ _)⟩
  choose t ht using glue
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := sectionsOver_exists_mk P H.obj (fun W hW => t ⟨W, hW⟩)
    fun W W' f hW hW' =>
      Sheaf.isSeparated H W' _ (reachSieve_mem hP h𝒜 hT₁ hW') _ _ fun Z g ⟨c⟩ => by
        rw [← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ← H.obj.map_comp, ← op_comp, ht ⟨W, hW⟩ Z (g ≫ f) c,
          ht ⟨W', hW'⟩ Z g c]
  refine ⟨y, sectionsComplex_ext T H.obj fun e => ?_⟩
  change (augmentation hT H.obj ≫ sectionsπ T H.obj 0 e) y = _
  rw [augmentation_π, hy]
  have := ht ⟨_, hT 0 e⟩ _ (𝟙 _) (ProHom.mk ⟨e, 𝟙 _⟩)
  rwa [op_id, H.obj.map_id, ConcreteCategory.id_apply, ProHom.eval_mk_id] at this

/-- **The Čech complex of an injective abelian sheaf is exact in positive degrees.** -/
theorem isZero_homology_sectionsComplex [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max u v}]
    (H : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{max u v}) [Injective H]
    (h𝒜 : ∀ B : C, Sieve.generate (fun (B' : C) (_ : B' ⟶ B) => 𝒜 B') ∈ J B)
    (hT₂ : ∀ B : C, 𝒜 B → IsProProductAt T B) (n : ℕ) (hn : 1 ≤ n) :
    IsZero ((sectionsComplex T H.obj).homology n) := by
  obtain ⟨m, rfl⟩ : ∃ m, n = m + 1 := ⟨n - 1, by omega⟩
  have : Injective H.obj := Sheaf.injective_obj H
  rw [← HomologicalComplex.exactAt_iff_isZero_homology,
    HomologicalComplex.exactAt_iff' _ m (m + 1) (m + 1 + 1) (by simp) (by simp),
    ShortComplex.ab_exact_iff]
  exact fun x hx => exists_d_eq_of_injective 𝒜 H.obj
    (mono_cofreeι 𝒜 H.obj (eq_zero_of_sheaf H h𝒜)) (fun B => hT₂ B.obj B.property) m x hx

/-- **The Čech complex of a pro-covering is a resolution for injective sheaves**: for an
injective abelian sheaf `H`, the augmentation `Γ_P(H) ⟶ (lim_e H(T(n)_e))_n` is a
quasi-isomorphism, i.e. `0 ⟶ Γ_P(H) ⟶ lim_e H(T(0)_e) ⟶ lim_e H(T(1)_e) ⟶ ⋯` is exact. -/
theorem quasiIso_augmentationMap [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max u v}]
    (H : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{max u v}) [Injective H]
    (hP : ∀ ⦃B' B : C⦄, (B' ⟶ B) → P B → P B') (hT : ∀ n e, P ((T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).obj e))
    (h𝒜 : ∀ B : C, Sieve.generate (fun (B' : C) (_ : B' ⟶ B) => 𝒜 B') ∈ J B)
    (hT₁ : ∀ B : C, 𝒜 B → P B → ∃ e, Nonempty (B ⟶ (T.obj (op ⦋0⦌)).obj e))
    (hT₂ : ∀ B : C, 𝒜 B → IsProProductAt T B) :
    QuasiIso (augmentationMap hT H.obj) := by
  refine ⟨fun n => ?_⟩
  cases n with
  | zero =>
    rw [CochainComplex.quasiIsoAt₀_iff, ShortComplex.quasiIso_iff_of_zeros]
    · refine (ShortComplex.exact_and_mono_f_iff_of_iso ?_).2
        ⟨augmentation_exact H hP hT h𝒜 hT₁ hT₂, mono_augmentation H hP hT h𝒜 hT₁⟩
      exact ShortComplex.isoMk (Iso.refl _) (Iso.refl _) (Iso.refl _)
        ((Category.id_comp _).trans (by
          simp only [augmentationMap, HomologicalComplex.shortComplexFunctor'_map_τ₂,
            CochainComplex.fromSingle₀Equiv_symm_apply_f_zero, Iso.refl_hom]
          exact (Category.comp_id _).symm))
        ((Category.id_comp _).trans (Category.comp_id _).symm)
    all_goals rfl
  | succ n =>
    rw [quasiIsoAt_iff_exactAt _ _ (CochainComplex.exactAt_succ_single_obj _ _),
      HomologicalComplex.exactAt_iff_isZero_homology]
    exact isZero_homology_sectionsComplex H h𝒜 hT₂ (n + 1) (by omega)

/-- **The Čech complex of a pro-covering is a resolution for injective sheaves**, with the
hypotheses stated at every object: the sieve of morphisms into an object with property `P`
whose source maps to `(T(0)_e)_e` covers, and every object satisfies the pro-product
condition.  This is `quasiIso_augmentationMap` for the objects which map to `(T(0)_e)_e` or do
not have property `P`. -/
theorem quasiIso_augmentationMap_of_forall [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max u v}]
    (H : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{max u v}) [Injective H]
    (hP : ∀ ⦃B' B : C⦄, (B' ⟶ B) → P B → P B') (hT : ∀ n e, P ((T.obj (op ⦋n⦌)).obj e))
    (hT₁ : ∀ B : C, P B → Sieve.generate
      (fun (B' : C) (_ : B' ⟶ B) => ∃ e, Nonempty (B' ⟶ (T.obj (op ⦋0⦌)).obj e)) ∈ J B)
    (hT₂ : ∀ B : C, IsProProductAt T B) :
    QuasiIso (augmentationMap hT H.obj) := by
  refine quasiIso_augmentationMap (𝒜 := fun B => P B → ∃ e, Nonempty
    (B ⟶ (T.obj (op ⦋0⦌)).obj e)) H hP hT (fun B => ?_) (fun B h𝒜 hB => h𝒜 hB)
    (fun B _ => hT₂ B)
  by_cases hB : P B
  · refine J.superset_covering ?_ (hT₁ B hB)
    rintro Z g ⟨B', a, f, hf, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨B', a, f, fun _ => hf, rfl⟩
  · have : Sieve.generate (fun (B' : C) (_ : B' ⟶ B) =>
        P B' → ∃ e, Nonempty (B' ⟶ (T.obj (op ⦋0⦌)).obj e)) = ⊤ :=
      (Sieve.id_mem_iff_eq_top).1 ⟨B, 𝟙 _, 𝟙 _, fun h => (hB h).elim, Category.id_comp _⟩
    rw [this]
    exact J.top_mem B

end Sheaf

end Stacks.ProCech
